 for the Boston Marathon, you have to run a fast time for your age."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob10aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to excite"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be filled with excitement or emotional energy"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It excites me to see so many international runners racing together."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob10aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to converge"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to come from various directions and meet together in one place"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The best runners in the world converge in Boston to run the marathon. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob10aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "elite"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the best in their sport or job"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Runners from Kenya are considered elites in the world."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob10aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "It's getting late"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "It's getting near the end of the day."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's getting late, so we should go home."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob10aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "seaside"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the area along the edge of the sea"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I love taking bike rides along the seaside."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob10aud07"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"ty